 "description": "Two probes before C.2's fit is registered (description, discarded seeds).\n\nBoth run on the package's procedure options (`c2_encoder_probe.PROCEDURE_SETTINGS`: per-ligand\ntying, the soft-capped readout with pool centres, the graded box with the inhibition floor at 0.09,\nPDFR-1's and SER-5's cited signs, slow speed noise). The guards read the network through\n`ConnectomeTopology.forward_observer`: a candidate with over half its motor neurons at |h| > 0.99\nin over half its steps scores 500 more; one whose speed or reversal output spans less than 0.5\nbetween its 5th and 95th percentiles over 8 recorded animals scores 300 more. Readouts every 10\ngenerations on the search's mean, on 200 animals, grade every family and the three Scheer mutants.\n\n**B01, a clean start.** From the graded box's centre, where every sensory gain is 0 and the network\ngets no input.\n- Stage 1 fits the 77 parameters that carry the senses to the outputs (the wiring, sensory, readout\n  and noise blocks and the pool centres), every other at the centre, on D_fit's families (small\n  lawn, uniform well, kinematics, activity), at sigma0 0.2, for 60 generations.\n- Stage 2 fits all 137 from stage 1's answer on all six families, at sigma0 0.1, for 100\n  generations.\n- Both at 64 animals a candidate (the stored 64-animal bands) and population 24.\n- The rules, fixed before the run: stop after stage 1 unless its last readout's outputs are\n  responsive (speed and reversal spread at least 0.5) and the worm is on the small lawn at least\n  0.75 of the time. Stop stage 2 at its generation 100 unless its readout D is below 3. The region is\n  reached if the last readout has D at most 2.5 with at least 3 families passing.\n\n**B02, tax-4 left out.** From Logbook 129's passing answer in the package's encoding, at sigma0\n0.02, the objective's six families plus tph-1's and pdfr-1's lawn differences, the two mutants\nweighted to half the objective, at 64 animals and population 24, for 40 generations. tax-4 is read\nat every readout, never fitted. The answer's own fit included tax-4, so this asks whether tax-4\nstays right once nothing holds it there: a proxy for prediction, not the held-out test itself. The\nrule, fixed before the run: stop at generation 40 if the readout D is more than 0.5 above its start\nor a fitted mutant fails.\n\nSeeds: B01's stage 1 on 810 M and stage 2 on 812 M (64\u00b7k + i), CMA 9490 and 9491; B02 on 815 M,\nCMA 9492; readouts on 811 M and 816 M (+ i, 200 animals). Run from the repository root:\n`probes.py B01` and `probes.py B02`, in parallel.\n",
